PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains a unanimous consensus on **B. The strength of genetic drift**. Mechanistically, as degraded genomic sequences shrink, their selective cost approaches zero and falls below the drift barrier ($|s| < 1/2N_e$), rendering purifying selection inoperative. Consequently, the stochastic persistence and residence time of these small near-neutral fragments are governed directly by random genetic drift rather than selective efficiency. Furthermore, demographic contractions in lineages undergoing genomic decay directly collapse $N_e$, establishing drift as the primary upstream driver. My position remains firmly anchored on Choice B.
}

